:"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"a flaw was found in the event-driven ansible (eda) server. the externaleventstreamviewset uses permissive access controls (permission_classes=[allowany], authentication_classes=[]) and relies solely on the subject http header value for mtls authentication without verifying that the header originated from a trusted proxy. additionally, the expected certificate distinguished name is leaked in the 403 error response body. an attacker who can reach the eda api endpoint with a spoofed subject header can inject arbitrary events into mtls-protected event streams, triggering downstream automation actions."},{"subject":"CVE-2026-12383","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat Ansible Automation Platform 2.5 for RHEL 8","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat ansible automation platform 2.5 for rhel 8"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-12383","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat Ansible Automation Platform 2.5 for RHEL 9","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat ansible automation platform 2.5 for rhel 9"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-12383","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat Ansible Automation Platform 2.6 for RHEL 9","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat ansible automation platform 2.6 for rhel 9"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-12383","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat Ansible Automation Platform 2.7","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat ansible automation platform 2.7"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-12383","predicate":"rdf:type","object":"Vulnerability","source":"cve","object_type":"enum","object_canonical":"vulnerability"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-12383","predicate":"related-weakness","object":"CWE-345","source":"cve","object_type":"id","object_canonical":"CWE-345"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-12383","predicate":"state","object":"PUBLISHED","source":"cve","object_type":"enum","object_canonical":"published"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-12383","predicate":"vendo