,"object_type":"string","object_canonical":"redhat"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-12701","predicate":"cvss-base-score","object":"9","source":"cve","object_type":"number","object_canonical":"9"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-12701","predicate":"cvss-severity","object":"CRITICAL","source":"cve","object_type":"enum","object_canonical":"critical"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-12701","predicate":"date-published","object":"2026-07-20T14:18:18.318Z","source":"cve","object_type":"date","object_canonical":"2026-07-20t14:18:18.318z"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-12701","predicate":"date-updated","object":"2026-11-02T17:14:10.935Z","source":"cve","object_type":"date","object_canonical":"2026-11-02t17:14:10.935z"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-12701","predicate":"description","object":"A path traversal vulnerability was found in pulpcore. The relative_path_validator function only verifies that content paths do not begin with \"/\" but fails to block directory traversal sequences such as \"../\" anywhere in the path. An authenticated administrator can craft a relative_path containing embedded traversal sequences (e.g., \"looking/normal/../../../../etc/shadow\") that escapes the intended export directory during FilesystemExport operations. Because the file content is also user-controlled (uploaded artifact), this allows arbitrary file write to any location writable by the Pulp service user, potentially leading to service compromise or further system exploitation.","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"a path traversal vulnerability was found in pulpcore. the relative_path_validator function only verifies that content paths do not begin with \"/\" but fails to block directory traversal sequences such as \"../\" anywhere in the path. an authenticated administrator can craft a relative_path containing embedded traversal sequences (e.g., \"looking/normal/../../../../etc/shadow\") that escapes the intended export directory during filesystemexport operations. because the file content is also user-controlled (uploaded artifact), this allows arbitrary file write to any location writable by the pulp service user, potentially leading to service compromise or further system exploitation."},{"subject":"CVE-2026-12701","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat Ansible Automation Platform 2.5 for RHEL 8","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat ansible automation platform 2.5 for rhel 8"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-12701","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat Ansible Automation Platform 2.5 for RHEL 9","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat ansible automation platform 2.5 for rhel 9"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-12701","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat Ansible Automation Platform 2.6 for RHEL 9","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat ansible automation platform 2.6 for rhel 9"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-12701","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat Satellite 6.16 for RHEL 8","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat satellite 6.16 for rhel 8"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-12701","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat Satellite 6.16 for RHEL 9","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat satellite 6.16 for rhel 9"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-12701","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat Satellite 6.17 for RHEL 9","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat satellite 6.17 for rhel 9"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-12701","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat Satellite 6.18 for RHEL 9","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat satellite 6.18 for rhel 9"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-12701","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat Satellite 6.19 for RHEL 9","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat satellite 6.19 for rhel 9"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-12701","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat Ansible Automation Platform 2.6","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat ansible automation platform 2.6"},{"s